Sdickers — Local Setup (macOS, Apple Silicon)
=============================================

Requirements:
  - Node.js 20+ (install from nodejs.org, or: brew install node)
  - A Supabase account (free) — the database and image storage are hosted there,
    so nothing to install locally.

Step 1 — Get your Supabase credentials
  1. Create a project at https://supabase.com (or use the existing one).
  2. Database URL: Dashboard -> Project Settings -> Database -> Connect -> Connection string (URI).
     Copy it and replace [YOUR-PASSWORD] with your database password.
  3. Frontend keys: Dashboard -> Project Settings -> API.
     Copy the Project URL and the anon/publishable key.

Step 2 — Configure the server
  cd server
  cp .env.example .env
  Then edit server/.env and fill in:
    DATABASE_URL     (from step 1.2)
    SECRET_KEY       (run: node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(48).toString('hex'))")
    ADMIN_EMAIL / ADMIN_PASSWORD / ADMIN_PHONE / ADMIN_USERNAME  (admin account
      that gets created automatically on first server start)
    EMAIL_USER / EMAIL_PASS (optional — Gmail app password for OTP emails)
  Note: if a password/value contains #, wrap the whole value in double quotes.

Step 3 — Configure the frontend
  cd frontend
  cp .env.example .env
  Then edit frontend/.env and fill in:
    VITE_SUPABASE_URL and VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY (from step 1.3)

Step 4 — Install dependencies
  cd server && npm install
  cd ../frontend && npm install

Step 5 — Create the database tables (one time only)
  cd server
  npx knex migrate:latest

Step 6 — Start the backend
  cd server
  npm start
  -> Server running on PORT 3000
  -> "Database connected successfully"
  (The admin account is created automatically on first start.)

Step 7 — Start the frontend (in a second terminal)
  cd frontend
  npm run dev
  -> Open http://localhost:5173

Admin login:
  Open http://localhost:5173/login and log in with the ADMIN_EMAIL /
  ADMIN_PASSWORD you set in server/.env. The site shows the admin panel
  (/admin) only to accounts with the admin role.

Stopping:
  Press Ctrl+C in each terminal.
